# grammar: v0 (unfrozen; AST normative)
#
# seidr — the magic system of the Norse world, as a declared PRACTICE (04). Seidr
# is the fate-craft: the volva weaves and reads the web the Norns spin, drawing on
# orlog (fate-debt owed) and on her own megin (bodily might). The kernel supplies
# one generic checker; this pack supplies the kinds, the resources, the roles, the
# laws, the failure classes refining L2..L6, and the currencies a working spends —
# all as data, zero kernel code (koan 10). It closes with a WORKED PROOF that
# HOLDS: one casting written out and checked against the practice and the scene.
scope seidr

use chronology        # a working seats its hour on the moon's wheel

# --- the pack's ledger --------------------------------------------------------
ratify d-0101   # the moon wheel the timing failure is seated on
ratify d-0104   # the seeress and the wanderer who meet in the worked proof
ratify d-0105   # the certain ground the proof's premises rest on

# --- cyclic time the practice needs: the moon's twenty-nine nights ------------
# The SAME rank-refusing cyclic kind the timing checker shares (03-time §1.iv):
# succ/pred/across/distance exist; `<`, sort, and max are type errors.
cycle moon(29)   decided d-0101

# --- the certain ground the worked proof rests on -----------------------------
# The seeress's standing to work seidr and the wanderer's consent to be answered
# are facts in the certain layer, so the proof's premises seat in the pool rather
# than fizzle (the seam of 04 §2: premises are the certain projection of a scene).
person the-seeress  "The Seeress"    decided d-0104
person the-wanderer "The Wanderer"   decided d-0104

standing(the-seeress)   decided d-0105
consent(the-wanderer)   decided d-0105

# --- the practice: a conserved fate-debt and an affine-bounded body (04 §3) ----
# Orlog is a LINEAR CONSERVED resource: a fate-debt drawn must balance across every
# close — nothing is minted or burned, only revealed, assigned, or settled. Megin
# is AFFINE BOUNDED: the seer's body caps the draw, overspend fails and underspend
# is legal. The failure classes refine L2..L6, including the licensed-ignorance
# shape only an annotated kernel can state (a seeing true against a licensed pool
# yet false against the certain). Hosts on the one generic checker, no kernel code.
practice seidr  proposed {
  use chronology.cycles                       # the working seats its hour on the moon
  kind working = prophecy | weather-witch | shape-sending
  role seer       : person   requires standing(seer)
  role petitioner : person   requires consent(petitioner)
  resource orlog  : linear conserved          # a fate-debt drawn must balance — the debt law
  resource megin  : affine bounded body-limit # the seer's body caps the draw
  rule weave(working, seer)
  rule spend-and-settle                       # every fate-debt revealed, assigned, or settled balances
  condition witnessed requires witness within earshot
  error unowed         refines L2 premise-not-available where absent
                       # a working drawn on a fate never granted
  error fate-denied    refines L2 premise-not-available where contradicted signals recoil
                       # a fate the Norns' web contradicts recoils on the seer
  error wrong-moon     refines L3 side-condition [timing] over cycle moon
                       # the same seeing, worked at the wrong turn of the moon
  error mislaid-working refines L4 bad-instantiation
                       # a working bound against a kind the practice does not carry
  error broken-thread  refines L5 invalid-chain
                       # a step joining premises the fate-craft does not license
  error overdrawn      refines L6 resource-violation on megin signals collapse
                       # drawing more might than the body-limit allows
  error hollow-seeing  refines L2 where available-in(licensed-pool) and contradicted-in(certain)
                       # seats-and-lies: true against a licensed pool, false against the certain
  cost fate | bodily | social | epistemic
  }

# --- a worked diegetic proof: one scene's reasoning, checked (04 §5) -----------
# The Wanderer (Odin in disguise) rides to the dead seeress and asks her the doom.
# Her standing to work and his consent to be answered seat in the pool; a fate-debt
# is drawn against her standing; the `weave` rule is instantiated for a prophecy;
# a `spend-and-settle` chain concludes the seeing; the orlog is settled so the
# linear-conserved debt balances to zero; and the close holds. The interior is
# captured clause text, checked by the proof lane against seidr, zero kernel code.
proof the-seeress-answers  speaker the-seeress  in seidr {
  premise p1  standing(the-seeress)   cited d-0105  cue "the Wanderer wakes her from the mound"
  premise p2  consent(the-wanderer)   cited d-0105
  premise p3  orlog(1)                drawn-against p1
  step   s1  instantiate weave  with working = prophecy, seer = the-seeress
  step   s2  chain from p1, s1 by spend-and-settle conclusion foretold(the-seeress, doom)
  spend  p3
  close  foretold(the-seeress, doom)  expect holds
  }
